comment: |-
  # Review: cargo-credential 0.4.9
  
  - Upstream: https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo (credential/cargo-credential)
  - Upstream commit: 840b83a10fb0e039a83f4d70ad032892c287570a
  - Verification: pass (source bit-for-bit identical)
  
  ## Code review findings
  
  **Thoroughness: medium** (653 LoC, 4 files, all read in full.)
  
  Official Cargo team crate from rust-lang/cargo. Implements the JSON credential helper
  protocol: CredentialHello → CredentialRequest → CredentialResponse.
  
  ### Non-negotiable checks
  
  - **build.rs**: None. Positive.
  - **Proc macros**: None (serde/thiserror derive are external). Positive.
  - **Dependencies**: serde, serde_json, thiserror, anyhow, time, libc (Unix),
    windows-sys (Windows). All justified.
  - **FFI**: Unix dup/dup2/close, Windows GetStdHandle/SetStdHandle — for console
    redirection during interactive credential prompts.
  - **`unsafe`**: Four blocks in stdio.rs, all standard POSIX/Win32 fd/handle manipulation
    with RAII guards for cleanup. Error-checked. Sound.
  
  ### Red-flag scan
  
  Clean. No network, no env vars, no process spawning. Opens /dev/tty (Unix) or CONIN$/
  CONOUT$ (Windows) for interactive prompts — justified. Secret<T> properly redacts
  values in Debug output.
  
  ### Architecture
  
  main() handles protocol loop: write hello → read request → redirect stdio to console
  (ReplacementGuard RAII) → call Credential::perform → write response. Error type
  supports full chain round-tripping through JSON serialization.
  
  ## Cross-check
  
  No prior reviews at any version.
  
  ## Rating rationale
  
  Positive: well-structured official Cargo crate, sound unsafe blocks, good security
  practices (Secret<T> redaction), comprehensive error handling with chain preservation.
