  process spawning, no FFI, no unsafe. Single dependency (memchr).
  
  ### Architecture
  
  `Matcher` trait: two required methods (find_at, new_captures), many default impls for
  iteration, captures, replacement. Uses internal iteration (push model) for performance.
  `interpolate` function handles `$N`/`$name`/`${name}` replacement references.
  Supporting types: Match (range), LineTerminator, ByteSet (256-bit), Captures trait.
  
  ## Rating rationale
  
  Strong: pure trait definition library from a well-known author, zero unsafe, zero
  dependencies beyond memchr, no I/O of any kind. Comprehensive default implementations
  with correct empty-match handling.
