  matches upstream tag v0.1.5 exactly. v0.1.5 is the latest release.
  
  Unix escaping uses sound single-quote wrapping with correct handling of
  embedded single quotes and csh ! history expansion. Whitelist approach
  for safe characters is conservative and appropriate.
  
  Windows escaping correctly implements the CommandLineToArgvW algorithm
  (backslash doubling before quotes, trailing backslash doubling). Note:
  does NOT escape cmd.exe metacharacters (%, ^, |, &, <, >) which is a
  known limitation of this approach, not a bug.
  
  Code originally derived from the Rust project (see copyright header).
  Author sfackler is a well-known Rust ecosystem contributor.
  
  No red flags. Recommend for use.
