  ## Code review findings
  
  **Thoroughness level: medium** — the crate is 106 Rust LoC (single file `src/lib.rs`), small enough to read carefully end-to-end.
  
  **Claims baseline:** The crate claims to provide a macro (`caret_int!`) for declaring non-exhaustive C-style enumerations — integer newtypes where some values have names and others are just raw integers. Part of the Arti/Tor ecosystem.
  
  ### File map
  
  - `src/lib.rs` (151 lines) — **read in full**
  - `tests/example_int.rs` (51 lines) — **read in full**
  - `Cargo.toml.orig` — **read in full**
  - `README.md` — **read in full**
  
