  - `#![no_std]` — no std at all.
  
  All clear. This is a trivially simple crate.
  
  ### Architecture summary
  
  This crate is a thin semver-trick shim. It depends on `webpki-roots` v1 (aliased as `parent`) and re-exports its single public item `TLS_SERVER_ROOTS`. The crate uses `#![no_std]` and `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`. There is no logic, no data, and no attack surface in this crate itself — all substance lives in the v1 crate.
  
