  ## External verification
  
  - Upstream repo: https://github.com/dbrgn/tracing-test
  - Upstream commit (from .cargo_vcs_info.json): 31f16ca7d635d02e6b2ed3ddbefe09164b262f2e
  - Tag v0.2.6 on upstream points to the same commit: confirmed
  - diff -r between crate and upstream at recorded commit: match (only .cargo-ok and Cargo.toml.orig differ, both are cargo artifacts)
  
  ## Code review findings
  
  ### Structure
  
  The crate has 3 source files totaling ~50 LoC of logic (excluding doc comments):
  
  - src/lib.rs: Almost entirely doc comments. Re-exports tracing_test_macro::traced_test and exposes internal and subscriber modules.
  - src/subscriber.rs: MockWriter struct wrapping &Mutex<Vec<u8>>, implements io::Write and MakeWriter. get_subscriber() builds a FmtSubscriber dispatch.
  - src/internal.rs: INITIALIZED: Once for one-time setup, global_buf() returning a OnceLock<Mutex<Vec<u8>>>, logs_with_scope_contain() and logs_assert() for test assertions.
  
  ### Companion proc-macro crate (tracing-test-macro =0.2.6)
  
  The #[traced_test] attribute macro (138 lines) injects:
  1. One-time global subscriber initialization
  2. A tracing span named after the test function (with counter for duplicates)
  3. logs_contain() and logs_assert() helper functions
  
  No surprising code generation. The macro only injects calls back into tracing_test::internal::*.
  
  ### Dependencies
  
  - tracing-core 0.1 (standard)
  - tracing-subscriber 0.3 with env-filter feature (standard)
  - tracing-test-macro =0.2.6 (companion proc-macro, pinned exact version)
  
  ### Safety / red flags
  
  - No unsafe blocks anywhere in the crate
  - No build.rs
  - No FFI / extern calls
  - No network access or file I/O (other than stdout via print!())
  - No ambient authority - the crate only operates on in-memory buffers
  - One unwrap() on String::from_utf8() for printing to stdout - acceptable for test-only code
  - Two unwrap() calls on mutex locks - standard pattern; poisoned mutex indicates prior panic
  
  ### Potential concerns (minor)
  
  1. Global mutable state (global_buf(), INITIALIZED) means all tests in a process share one log buffer. By design; scope-based filtering handles separation.
  2. print!() in MockWriter::write() means logs go to both stdout and the buffer. Intentional for cargo test capture behavior.
  
  ### Malicious intent assessment
  
  No indicators of malicious behavior. The code is straightforward, does exactly what it claims, and has no capability to access anything beyond in-memory buffers and stdout.
  
  ## Cross-check
  
  No existing cargo-crev reviews found for tracing-test.
  
  ## Open questions
  
  - Did not audit transitive dependencies (tracing-subscriber, tracing-core, quote, syn).
  - Did not separately verify tracing-test-macro crate on crates.io matches upstream at same commit (only verified tracing-test itself). The exact version pin =0.2.6 ensures they are published together.
