  ## Code review findings
  
  Thoroughness level: **medium** (bordering high). Justification: the crate has only 2 lines of Rust code (excluding the doc comment), so a complete end-to-end read is trivial.
  
  ### File map
  
  - `lib.rs` — **read in full**. 21 lines total: a module-level doc comment (lines 1–17), `#![no_std]` (line 19), and `pub extern crate jiff_tzdb;` (line 21).
  - `Cargo.toml` / `Cargo.toml.orig` — **read in full**.
  - `README.md` — **read in full**.
  - `COPYING`, `LICENSE-MIT`, `UNLICENSE` — license files, not read (standard BurntSushi triple-license).
