  ### Architecture summary
  
  This is a trivially simple crate. It declares `#![no_std]` and publicly re-exports the `jiff_tzdb` crate. The entire Rust source is two meaningful lines. The crate exists purely as an indirection layer for Cargo's target-specific dependency resolution — Jiff depends on this crate only on Windows, which causes `jiff-tzdb` (the actual data) to be pulled in only on platforms that need it.
  
  ### Claims vs reality reconciliation
  
  The crate claims to be a re-export proxy for `jiff-tzdb` on specific platforms. The code does exactly that — `pub extern crate jiff_tzdb;` — and nothing more. No capabilities are exercised beyond the re-export. `#![no_std]` confirms no standard library usage. The single dependency (`jiff-tzdb`) is exactly what's expected. The code matches the claims perfectly.
  
