    - `WriteBytesExt` trait (lines 560–1066): Extension trait on `io::Write`. Each method
      converts via `ByteOrder` into a fixed-size buffer, then calls `write_all`. Same
      uniform pattern. Blanket impl for all `io::Write`.
  
  ### Claims vs. reality reconciliation
  
  The crate claims: pure byte-order conversion, no unsafe, no_std support. Reality
  matches exactly. No network, filesystem, process, or env access. Zero dependencies.
  The `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` attribute is present and enforced.
  
